*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Molecule: Oxygen (O2), triplet
* Basis: cc-pVDZ
* Symmetry: C1
* Features tested: shared GATEWAY/SEWARD, SCF(UHF), MBPT2(UMP2, FC2),
*                  RASSCF(ROHF), MBPT2(ROMP2, FC2)
* Responsible person: Okan Koeksal
* Comments: UMP2 and semicanonical ROMP2 for the same oxygen geometry and
*           conventional AO integrals. The RunFile is restored after UMP2
*           so that the RASSCF reference starts from the SEWARD state.
*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
>> export MOLCAS_PRINT=VERBOSE
>> export MOLCAS_MEM=512

&GATEWAY
Title
O2 UMP2 and ROMP2 C1 conventional FC2
Coord
2
O2 fixed geometry, angstrom
O 0.0 0.0  0.61150
O 0.0 0.0 -0.59650
Basis set
cc-pVDZ
Group = NoSym

&SEWARD

* Preserve the integral-generation RunFile
>> COPY $Project.RunFile $Project.BaselineRunFile

* UHF -> UMP2, two frozen occupied orbitals
&SCF
UHF
Occupied
9
7

&MBPT2
Frozen
2

* Restore the common pre-SCF reference for an independent ROHF calculation
>> COPY $Project.BaselineRunFile $Project.RunFile

* Determinant RASSCF/ROHF -> semicanonical ROMP2, FC2
&RASSCF
Symmetry = 1
Spin = 3
Frozen = 0
Inactive = 7
Nactel = 2 0 0
Ras2 = 2
Deleted = 0
Ciroot = 1 1 1

&MBPT2
Frozen
2
End of input
